<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuania 182-day T-bill rate climbs.</title>
<headline>Lithuania 182-day T-bill rate climbs.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield at an auction of Lithuanian Treasury bills climbed on Tuesday, reaching 11.53 percent after 9.76 percent previously, the central bank said.</p>
<p>All amounts are in millions of litas.</p>
<p> MATURITY   AV YIELD  LAST TIME   MIN/MAX   ISSUE  BID    SOLD</p>
<p>  182-day    11.53     9.76     10.85/12.41  40   37.344  33.344</p>
<p>The settlement date for today's auction was February 21 and the bills mature on August 22. The next auction is on February 24 when 50 million litas of 91-day paper will be sold and on February 25 when 40 million litas of 91-day will be offered. -- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
